Subject: [PATCH] esp32s3: pair BLE controller kernel allocations with kmm_free

The controller's malloc and malloc_internal callbacks both use kmm_malloc,
but its free callback uses the user-heap free. The OSI callback table is also
kernel-allocated and user-freed during teardown. With a separate kernel heap,
these pairs are invalid; without one the allocator aliases hide the problem.

Reproduced on ESP32-S3 with NuttX 13.1.0, PSRAM user heap and Wi-Fi/BLE enabled:
changing advertising data frees an internal-RAM controller allocation through
the PSRAM user heap and asserts mm_heapmember in mm_free. JTAG identifies the
controller's advertising-data handler as the caller. Use the matching kernel
deallocator on both paths, without changing allocation policy or radio APIs.

diff --git a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_ble_adapter.c b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_ble_adapter.c
--- a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_ble_adapter.c
+++ b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_ble_adapter.c
@@ -525,7 +525,7 @@ static struct osi_funcs_s g_osi_funcs =
   ._cause_sw_intr_to_core = NULL,
   ._malloc = malloc_wrapper,
   ._malloc_internal = malloc_internal_wrapper,
-  ._free = free,
+  ._free = kmm_free,
   ._read_efuse_mac = read_mac_wrapper,
   ._srand = srand_wrapper,
   ._rand = rand_wrapper,
@@ -2596,7 +2596,7 @@ static void bt_controller_deinit_internal(void)
 
   if (g_osi_funcs_p != NULL)
     {
-      free(g_osi_funcs_p);
+      kmm_free(g_osi_funcs_p);
       g_osi_funcs_p = NULL;
     }
 
